## ParseIntError / ParseFloatError — error classes returned by the
## `String#parse_int` / `String#parse_float` Result. The class shells
## are NOT in `register_builtins` (typeck constructs `Ty::Class { name:
## "ParseIntError" }` on the fly), so anchor mode does not apply here —
## these `class` decls register fresh DefKind::Class entries the
## ordinary way. The single `message` method on each maps to the same
## shared `ruxen_parse_error_message` runtime symbol.
class ParseIntError
  lib "runtime/string.c"
    def message as "ruxen_parse_error_message" -> String
  end
end
